// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO1 (SCL1) and GPIO2 (SDA1) - this board's
// pins_arduino.h declares a SECOND I2C bus (Wire1) distinct from the
// primary SDA=12/SCL=13 pins. Confirmed via the upstream arduino-esp32
// pull request that added this board
// (github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/pull/8257, "Add board: Nebula S3"
// by DocMonster7, merged 2023-05-31): the board carries an onboard
// MPU-6050 IMU wired to this secondary I2C bus specifically (commit
// history: "add secondary sda1 and scl1" alongside the IMU addition),
// plus an onboard WS2812B addressable LED and a battery connector.
// Also corroborated by PlatformIO's board listing
// (docs.platformio.org/en/latest/boards/espressif32/nebulas3.html,
// "Kinetic Dynamics Nebula S3"). Per the pin-audit playbook, a
// communication bus wired exclusively to a specific onboard chip is
// EXCLUDE (dedicated), unlike a general-purpose I2C header - this is
// the dedicated-IMU case, so GPIO1/GPIO2 are removed from chipGpios.
// The primary SDA=12/SCL=13 (Wire0) pins are general-purpose and kept.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO45 tagged "led_neopixel" - this board's
// pins_arduino.h declares
// `static const uint8_t LED_BUILTIN = SOC_GPIO_PIN_COUNT + 45;` with
// RGB_BUILTIN/RGB_BRIGHTNESS also defined, which is the arduino-esp32
// convention for an onboard addressable RGB LED driven via
// neopixelWrite()/rgbLedWrite() rather than digitalWrite() - the real
// GPIO is the offset from SOC_GPIO_PIN_COUNT (49 for ESP32-S3, per
// esp-idf soc/esp32s3/include/soc/soc_caps.h), i.e. GPIO45. This matches
// the same encoding pattern used by variants/esp32/esp32s3/waveshare_esp32_s3_zero
// (`LED_BUILTIN = SOC_GPIO_PIN_COUNT + WS_RGB` where WS_RGB=21, already
// tagged led_neopixel there). Confirmed onboard WS2812B LED via the
// upstream PR (github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/pull/8257) and
// PlatformIO board listing. digital_input dropped from GPIO45's
// capabilities (dedicated LED data line), pwm_output retained because
// it was already present on this pin in the chip-level default.
